"subs": [
{
"t": 0.0,
"dur": 7.09,
"text": "Welcome! A three-generation home, keeping the old quarter's soul alive. Two million dong a night. Altar photos, fifty thousand dong extra."
},
{
"t": 7.34,
"dur": 7.17,
"text": "Keeping the old quarter's soul alive by charging admission to see an altar. Great-great-grandpa would charge you too."
},
{
"t": 14.91,
"dur": 6.643,
"text": "Sixty billion dong. Gut the whole inside. Keep the mossy gate for Western tourists to photograph as heritage."
},
{
"t": 21.803,
"dur": 2.124,
"text": "Sign! Gut the kitchen too, for all I care."
},
{
"t": 25.478,
"dur": 3.322,
"text": "Sell the house, and the house's things leave. I have to keep them here."
},
{
"t": 29.601,
"dur": 5.973,
"text": "Great-great-grandpa gave me one job: our whole fortune's in the jar under the kitchen. Guard it. So I did."
},
{
"t": 36.174,
"dur": 3.505,
"text": "And it really guarded the house. How? Full story on the channel."
}
],
